    en: 'Agriculture works through relationships. Soil, water, plants, animals, labour, knowledge, money, and markets exchange resources and create effects that may appear immediately or after several seasons. A farm decision should therefore be judged by more than yield alone. Food security, income, labour burden, soil condition, water use, risk, and the next season all belong in the assessment.\n\nThe practical habit is simple but powerful: map the system, identify the scarce resource, record an indicator, act at the right time, and review the result. This approach respects farmer experience while adding evidence that can be shared, compared, and improved. It is useful on a small Ethiopian mixed farm, a modern commercial plot, or any farm where decisions affect the land and future livelihood.',
